PANIC CODE      ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
----------      -------         --------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 7 ******


7300            STRP            AOS/VS TOOK A PROTECTION FAULT
                                 INSIDE THE SYSTEM.
                                VALUE #1= AC0 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #2= AC1 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #3= AC2 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #4= FP @ TRAP
                                VALUE #5= PC OF INSTRUCTION CAUSING TRAP
                                VALUE #6= TRAP CODE

                                        0 READ VIOLATION
                                        1 WRITE VIOLATION
                                        2 EXECUTE VIOLATION
                                        3 VALIDITY PROTECTION (SBR OR PTE)
                                        4 INWARD ADDRESS REFERENCE
                                        5 DEFER (INDIRECT) VIOLATION
                                        6 ILLEGAL GATE
                                        7 OUTWARD CALL
                                        10 INWARD RETURN
                                        11 PRIVILEGED INSTRUCTION
                                        12 I/O PROTECTION VIOLATION
                                        13 *NOT DEFINED*
                                        14 INVALID MICROINTERRUPT RETURN BLOCK
                                        15 UNIMPLEMENTED INSTRUCTION

                                VALUE #7= ADDRESS CAUSING TRAP
                                VALUE #8= INTERRUPT LEVEL

7301            FPFLT           AOS/VS SYSTEM FLOATING POINT FAULT
                                VALUE #1= AC0 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #2= AC1 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #3= AC2 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #4= FP @ TRAP
                                VALUE #5= PC OF INSTRUCTION CAUSING TRAP
                                VALUE #6= PSR ( SEE HDWR SPEC)
                                VALUE #7= HIGH ORDER HALF OF FP STATUS
                                VALUE #8= LOW ORDER HALF OF FP STATUS

7302            COMFLT          AOS/VS SYSTEM COMMERCIAL INSTR. FAULT
                                AS ABOVE EXCEPT
                                VALUE #7= COMMERCIAL FAULT TYPE (SEE HDWR SPEC)
                                VALUE #8= UNUSED

7303            FIXOV           AOS/VS SYSTEM FIXED POINT OVERFLOW
                                AS ABOVE EXCEPT
                                VALUE #7= UNUSED
                                VALUE #8= UNUSED

7304            STRAP           BEFORE GOING TO A CB FAULT HANDLER
                                ON A VALIDITY TRAP (IF A HANDLER
                                IS DEFINED) THIS CODE IS PUT IN 
                                THE PANIC CODE REGISTER. IF THE
                                HANDLER FINDS THAT IT CANNOT HANDLE
                                THE TRAP IT XJMPS TO STRP AND TAKES THIS
                                PANIC.
                                VALUE #5= PC THAT CAUSED THE TRAP
                                VALUE #6= TRAP CODE
                                VALUE #7= ADDRESS OF TRAP HANDLER
                                VALUE #8= INTLV

7305            PGFLT           WHEN A CONTROL BLOCK TAKES A FAULT
                                ON A USER PAGE AND THAT FAULT TAKES
                                AN ERROR DURING THE RESOLUTION THE
                                PAGE FAULT HANDLER WILL FORMAT A
                                TRAP AND THEN TRY TO THE TRAP
                                REDIRECTION ADDRESS SPECIFIED BY CBFEH
                                IN THE CB.  IF NONE IS SUPPLIED OR THE
                                THE REDIRECTION HANDLER CAN'T HANDLE
                                THE ERROR THIS PANIC OCCURS.

                                VALUE #1-#4= AC'S 0-3
                                VALUE #5= PC THAT CAUSED FAULT
                                VALUE #6= ERROR CODE FROM FAULT
                                VALUE #7= CBFEH FOR CB
                                VALUE #8= LOGICAL ADDRESS THAT CAUSED
                                          THE FAULT
