-----   -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 10 ******

10001   SHUTPR          [OBSOLETE]
                        OP CLI TRAPPED DUE TO A MAP VIOLATION
                                  VALUE #1= ACO @ TRAP
                                  VALUE #2= AC1 @ TRAP
                                  VALUE #3= AC2 @ TRAP
                                  VALUE #4= AC3 @ TRAP
                                  VALUE #5= C+PC @ TRAP
                                  VALUE #6 = HARDWARE TRAP CODE
                                        SEE PANIC 7300 DOCUMENTATION FOR
                                        A DESCRIPTION OF HARDWARE TRAP CODES

        NOTE THAT BECAUSE THE SYSTEM IS PROPERLY SHUT DOWN,  EVEN
                THOUGH THE PANIC 10001 OCCURRED, NEITHER ESD NOR
                FIXUP NEED BE RUN PRIOR TO BOOTING AGAIN.


10002   UCTD.P          PID 2 (OP:CLI) TERMINATED DUE TO AN MV/ECLIPSE
                        PROTECTION VIOLATION
                                   VALUES -- SAME AS PANIC #7300
                        UNLIKE PANIC 10001 [WHICH THIS REPLACES] THE SYSTEM
                        HAS NOT ATTEMPTED TO SHUT DOWN.

10003   UCTD.P          INITAL LOAD 'PROCESS' (CLIBT;PID 3) TERMINATED DUE
                        TO AN MV/ECLIPSE PROTECTION VIOLATION
                                   VALUES -- SAME AS PANIC #7300



PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 11 ******

11001    SMOND                  WHEN AOS/VS IS IDLE, IT CALCULATES A CHECK-
                                  SUM ON THE CONTENTS OF PARTS OF SYSTEM
                                  PAGE ZERO.  THESE LOCATIONS CONTAIN
                                  CONSTANTS WHICH DO NOT CHANGE ONCE THE
                                  SYSTEM HAS BEEN "BOOTED".   AN
                                  ERROR HAS OCCURRED WHERE THE CALCU-
                                  LATED CHECKSUM DOES NOT AGREE WITH
                                  THE GOOD CHECKSUM.

                                  VALUE #1=  GOOD CHECKSUM
                                  VALUE #2=  CALCULATED CHECKSUM
                                  VALUE #3=  (NOT RELEVANT)

11002    SMOND                  DURING THE CHECKSUMMING OF MEMORY,
                                  EACH MEMORY LOCATION IS READ TWICE
                                  THEN COMPARED TO VERIFY THAT BOTH
                                  READ'S ARE THE SAME PRIOR TO ADDING
                                  THE VALUE TO THE CHECKSUM VALUE BEING
                                  CALCULATED.   THE TWO READ'S OF THE
                                  SAME MEMORY LOCATION DID NOT AGREE.

                                  VALUE #1=  2ND "READ" VALUE
                                  VALUE #2=  1ST "READ" VALUE
                                  VALUE #3=  LOGICAL ADDRESS BEING READ


PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
------  -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 12 ******

12001   OSER                    THE PMGR IS TRYING TO SET INPUT DONE
                                  TWICE WHILE UNBLOCKING A "READ ECHO".

12002   UBLK                    THE DCU HAS BEEN TIMED FOR APPROX 5
                                  SECONDS WITHOUT UNLOCKING ITS "LOCK"
                                  WORD.   WOULD NORMALLY INDICATE THAT
                                  THE DCU HAS STOPPED FOR HARDWARE OR
                                  SOFTWARE REASONS.

12003   UBLK                    A COUNTER USED WHILE "UNBLOCKING" HAS
                                  BEEN FOUND TO BE INCONSISTANT.

12004   UBLK                    AN ATTEMPT HAS BEEN MADE TO SET EITHER
                                  INPUT OR OUTPUT DONE WHEN IT HAS
                                  ALREADY BEEN SET.

12005   MXMD                    A ROUTINE WHICH HANDLES MODEM INTERRUPTS
                                  IS ATTEMPTING TO SET INPUT DONE TWICE.

12006   MXMD                    A ROUTINE WHICH HANDLES MODEM INTERRUPTS
                                  IS ATTEMPTING TO SET OUTPUT DONE
                                  TWICE.

12007   HDCU                    DURING A MODEM DISCONNECT WITH A DCU,
                                  AN ATTEMPT HAS BEEN MADE TO TERMINATE
                                  THE ROOT PROCESS WHICH IS INDIC-
                                  ATED AS THE FATHER.

                                  VALUE #1= 0 ( FATHER'S PID - PDAD )
                                  VALUE #2= CONSOLE PORT # (PCONL)
                                  VALUE #3= PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS

12010   TERM                    THE PMGR TRAPPED DUE TO A PROTECTION
                                FAULT.
                                  ************************************
                                  IN AOS/VS, A SEPARATE CODE IS DEFINED
                                  FOR PANICS IN THE PMGR CONTEXT.
                                  ************************************

                                VALUE #1= AC0 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #2= AC1 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #3= AC2 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #4= AC3 @ TRAP
                                VALUE #5= C+PC @ TRAP
                                VALUE #6= FAULT CODE (SEE HDWR SPEC)
                                VALUE #7= ADDRESS THAT CAUSED TRAP
                                VALUE #8= INTERRUPT LEVEL AT TIME OF TRAP


IN AOS/VS, THESE CODES APPLY TO PANIC 012300 OR 017002:

        IN GENERAL PANIC VALUES 1-5 ARE:

        VALUE #1=       PANIC SUBCODE
        VALUE #2-#5     AC0,1,2,3 AT TRAP

        IF TRAP INVOLVES A SYSTEM CALL ERROR, VALUE #2 WOULD 
        GENERALLY = SYSTEM CALL ERROR CODE.

PMGR ERROR       PMGR
CODE NUMBER     MODULE                  DESCRIPTION
-----------     ------  ------------------------------------------------

        1       CARD    DATA OUT OF RANGE DURING BINARY PACKING CARD DATA
        2       CONCOM  MORE THAN 2**16 ?IREC ERRORS
        3       CONCOM  ERROR ON ?XLATE SYSTEM CALL WHILE ASSIGNING
                        INPUT RING BUFFER
        4       CONCOM  ERROR ON ?XLATE SYSTEM CALL WHILE ASSIGNING
                        OUTPUT RING BUFFER
        5       CONCOM  ERROR ON ?SGNL SYSTEM CALL WHILE ASSIGNING A
                        CONSOLE
        6       CONCOM  ATTEMPT TO RELEASE A PIB NOT ON OWNERS PIB
                        CHAIN
        15      CONCOM  ERROR ON ?SGNL CALL UPON COMPLETION OF PTERM
                        OR CHAIN PROCESSING
        16      CONCOM  ERROR WHILE WAKING UP PMGR TIMER ROUTINE
                        (JSR @.WAKE)
        17      CONCOM  ERROR FROM ?DELAY SYSTEM CALL WHILE WAITING
                        FOR DELIMITER TABLE MEMORY
        20      CONCOM  UNOWNED PIB FOUND DURING ?SEND PROCESSING
        21      CONCOM  ATTEMPTING TO SET DONE BIT TWICE WHILE
                        TERMINATING READ REQUESTS ENQUEUED BY A TASK
                        ON A SPECIFIC DEVICE(RTERM)
        22      CONCOM  SAME AS 21 EXCEPT ERROR ENCOUNTERED DURING
                        WRITE KILL PROCESSING
        23      LOCK    IOP FAILED TO UNLOCK.
        25      INIT    ERROR ON ?SUSER CALL
        26      INIT    ERROR ON ?PNAME CALL
