PANIC CODE 12, CONTINUED:  AOS/VS SPECIFIC CODES

12300    PMGRP                  PANIC PASSED FROM PMGR CONTEXT.
                                  PMGR PANIC CODE, AS DEFINED ABOVE,
                                  IS PASSED AS VALUE #1.
12301    DPMGR                  LPHY ERROR ON PIB OR DEVICE TABLE
                                  ADDRESS.
12302    DPMGR                  LPHY ERROR ON AGENT SEGMENT BASE ADDR.
12303    DPMGR                  LPHY ERROR ON PMGR SEGMENT BASE ADDR.
12304    UNBLK                  GETPHYS ERROR ON PMGR PAGE 0
12305    IOPDR                  GETPHYS ERROR ON PMGR PAGE 0
12306    PANIC                  LPMGR passed wrong number of panic args
12307    PRCNG                  THE PMGR was terminated by AOSVS
                                VALUE #1= Term error code

PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 13 ******

13001   IERCC                     THE MOS MEMORIES HAVE A FEATURE CALLED
                                  ERROR CHECKING AND CORRECTION (ERCC).
                                  THERE IS A FIVE BIT "CHECK FIELD"
                                  CONSTRUCTED EACH TIME A WORD IS WRIT-
                                  TEN.   THE "CHECK FIELD" IS RE-CON-
                                  STRUCTED AND COMPARED WITH THE ORIG-
                                  INAL FIELD EACH TIME THE MEMORY WORD
                                  IS READ.  IN THIS CASE, A MULTI-BIT
                                  ERCC ERROR HAS BEEN DETECTED BY THE
                                  HARDWARE FROM WHICH THE SOFTWARE CAN-
                                  NOT RECOVER.

                                  VALUE #1= HARDWARE DIA STATUS WORD
                                  VALUE #2= HARDWARE DIB STATUS WORD

                                  USING THE FORMATS FOR THE ABOVE WORDS
                                  FROM THE APPROPRIATE HARDWARE MANUAL,
                                  THE FAILING MEMORY CAN BE DETERMINED.

        NOTE THAT:
                A)  ERCC ERRORS WHICH CAUSE A "PANIC 13" ARE NOT
                        LOGGED IN "SYSLOG".
                B)  WHEN TROUBLE-SHOOTING THIS TYPE PROBLEM, "SYSLOG"
                        SHOULD BE CHECKED TO DETERMINE IF ANY SOFT
                        (RECOVERABLE SINGLE-BIT) ERRORS WERE RECORDED.
                C)  NO SINGLE-BIT ERRORS WILL BE RECORDED IN "SYSLOG"
                        UNLESS IT HAD BEEN "STARTED".


13002   FAULT                   THE HARDWARE/MICRO-CODE HAS DETECTED
                                A MULTI-BIT ERCC ERROR AND GENERATED
                                A PAGE FAULT TO NOTIFY THE OS.

                                VALUE #1= PHYSICAL PAGE NUMBER
                                VALUE #2= D-WORD ON MEMORY MODULE
                                VALUE #3= SYNDROME BITS

PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         ------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 14 ******

14001    BRKPT                  A HARDWARE BREAKPOINT HAS BEEN EXECUTED
                                  WHICH IS PRESENTLY AN UNSUPPORTED
                                  FEATURE UNDER AOS/VS.   LOCATION 12
                                  CONTAINS THE ADDRESS OF THIS PANIC TO
                                  PRESENTLY CATCH ANY WILD JUMPS.
                                
                                  VALUE #1=  ------       AS THEY WERE
                                  VALUE #2=       |---      AT TIME
                                  VALUE #3=  ------         OF JUMP

14002   TERM                    AN ERROR RETURN HAS BEEN TAKEN FROM
                                  RCORE ( RELEASE UNSHARED CORE, MAPS
                                  AND EXTENDER ).   SINCE RCORE NEVER
                                  TAKES THE ERROR RETURN,  THE PANIC
                                  SHOULD NEVER OCCUR.

14003    PCALL                  THE "LDSP" INSTRUCTION HAS FALLEN
                                  THROUGH INDICATING THAT THE RANGE
                                  INPUT VIA AC0 WAS NOT WITHIN THE
                                  ACCEPTABLE LIMITS.

                                  VALUE #1=  LDSP SOURCE (AC0)
                                  VALUE #2=  PROCESS TABLE STATUS
                                                WORD (PSTAT)

14004   IOCAL                   A ?SPAGE/?WRB/?RDB REQUEST HAS BEEN
                                  MADE FOR A SYNCHRONOUS LINE.   THESE
                                  ARE NOT APPLICABLE SYSTEM CALLS.

14005   IOCAL                   SAME AS "14004" EXCEPT THAT THE I/O
                                  ENQUEUE ROUTINE IS TRYING TO BE 
                                  CALLED.

14006   GPTBL                   THE PID THAT WAS PASSED TO THE "GET
                                  PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS" ROUTINE
                                  IS GREATER THAN THE LENGTH OF THE
                                  PID TABLE (PIDLN).

                                  VALUE #1= PASSED PID
                                  VALUE #2= PID TABLE LENGTH
                                  VALUE #3= (NOT RELEVANT)

14007   GPTBL                   THE PID THAT WAS PASSED TO THE "GET
                                  PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS" ROUTINE WAS
                                  FOR AN "UNUSED PID", IE: THE ENTRY
                                  IN PIDTB IS "0".

                                  VALUE #1= PASSED PID
                                  VALUE #2= 0 (PIDTB ENTRY FOR PID)
                                  VALUE #3= PIDTB ENTRY ADDRESS

14010   GCMEA                   THERE IS A CORE MAP ENTRY (CME) FOR
                                  EACH MEMORY PAGE THAT EXISTS IN AN
                                  AOS/VS SYSTEM.   THE ROUTINE MAPS THE
                                  CME INTO LOGICAL ADDRESS SPACE.
                                  THE LOGICAL PAGE # THAT WAS ASKED
                                  TO BE MAPPED WAS GREATER THAN THE
                                  HIGHEST EXISTING MEMORY PAGE (HPAGE).

                                  VALUE #1= HPAGE
                                  VALUE #2= REQUESTED PHYS PAGE #
                                  VALUE #3= (NOT RELEVANT)

14011   TRTN3                   A CHECK IS MADE TO ENSURE THAT THE
                                  PHYSICAL PAGE CONTAINING THE PROCESS
                                  TABLE EXTENDER IS THE SAME AS CON-
                                  TAINED IN CUR60.  THIS IS DONE AT THE
                                  END OF CONTROL BLOCK PROCESSING.  THEY
                                  ARE NOT THE SAME.

                                  VALUE #1= PAGE MASK FOR "AND"
                                  VALUE #2= CUR60 PHYS PAGE
                                  VALUE #3= PHYS PAGE CONTAINING EXTENDER

14012   LPBIS                   AN INTERRUPT HAS OCCURRED FROM THE DCH
                                  LINE PRINTER (LPB) AND THE STATUS
                                  INDICATES IT TO BE "OFF-LINE".   THE
                                  LPB DIC WHEN 2'S COMPLEMENTED SHOWS
                                  AN INCOMPLETE TRANSFER BUT THE BUFFER
                                  HEADER BYTE COUNT WHEN UPDATED SHOWS
                                  A COMPLETE TRANSFER.

                                  VALUE #1= 0
                                  VALUE #2= 0
                                  VALUE #3= LPB DCT ADDRESS

14013   DEBLK                   A CHECK IS MADE IN THE DEBLK ROUTINE
                                  AND THE USE COUNT OF THE BUFFER
                                  HEADER CONTAINING A "MAP" BLOCK
                                  IS FOUND TO BE GREATER THAN "1".

                                  VALUE #1= USE COUNT (BQUSC)
                                  VALUE #2= MAP BLOCK LOW DISK ADDR
                                  VALUE #3= BUFFER HEADER ADDRESS

14014    DPAST                  THE CDC (3330) DISK STARTUP ROUTINE
                                  IS ATTEMPTING TO START I/O ON A
                                  DISK FOR WHICH I/O HAS ALREADY BEEN
                                  STARTED.

14015    DPAST                  THE CDC (3330) DISK STARTUP ROUTINE
                                  USES THE "LDSP" INSTRUCTION TO GO
                                  FROM DISK STATE TO DISK STATE.  THE
                                  "STATE" SPECIFIED TO THE "LDSP"
                                  INSTRUCTION IS GREATER THAN THE
                                  DISPATCH TABLE (APPROX 0-15 OCTAL).

                                  VALUE #1= ERRORONOUS "STATE"

14016    DPDST                  SAME AS "14014" EXCEPT FOR A 6045/
                                  4234/6030/6070 TYPE DISK DRIVE.

14017    DPDST                  SAME AS "14015" EXCEPT FOR A 6045/
                                  4234/6030/6070 TYPE DISK DRIVE.

14020   GCHAIN                  SAME AS "14002".

14021   LPBIO                   THIS ROUTINE FORMATS A BUFFER HEADER
                                  FOR THE DATA CHANNEL LPB/LPD I/O
                                  REQUEST AND ENQUEUES IT TO THE
                                  PROPER DCT.  ON SETTING THE BYTE
                                  COUNT, A ERRONEOUS "COMPLETION"
                                  IS INDICATED.

                                  VALUE #3= LPB/LPD DCT ADDRESS

14022   LPBIO                   SAME AS "14021".


14023   ECC                     THE DISK ECC HANDLER IS ATTEMPTING
                                  TO MAP THE PHYS PAGE CONTAINING
                                  THE ERROR WORD INTO THE 66K SLOT.
                                  ON WHICH AN ERROR OCCURRED.

                                  VALUE #1= 0
                                  VALUE #2= PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #3= MAPPED 66K SLOT ADDRESS
                                                OF ERROR WORD

14024    DKTM                   A FIXED HEAD DISK UDB THAT IS BEING
                                  TIMED FOR 3 SEC HAS TIMED OUT.  THE
                                  ADDRESS OF THE UDB THAT "TIMED OUT"
                                  IS NOT THE ADDRESS OF THE CURRENT
                                  UDB.

                                  VALUE #1= CURRENT UDB ADDR (DCCRQ)
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= TIMED OUT UDB ADDRESS

14025   MCTIS                   THE MCA TRANSMIT STATE "LDSP" INSTR-
                                  UCTION FAILED.  PRESENTLY, THE
                                  LEGITIMATE STATES ARE 0-7.

                                  VALUE #1= STATE FOR "LDSP"

14026   MCRIS                   THE MCA RECEIVE STATE "LDSP" INSTRUC-
                                  TION FAILED.  PRESENTLY, THE
                                  LEGITIMATE STATES ARE 0-3.

                                  VALUE #1= RCVR STATUS (DIC)
                                  VALUE #2= STATE FOR "LDSP"
                                  VALUE #3= DCT ADDRESS

14027   SYDBL                   A CALL TO THE "DISABLE SYNC LINE"
                                  OVERLAY (SYDBL) HAS BEEN MADE.
                                  IT CALLED THE OVERLAY "CRBUF"
                                  TO RETURN A BUFFER ON WHICH AN
                                  ERROR RETURN WAS TAKEN.

14030   UCLOSE                  AN LOGICAL DISK IS BEING "CLOSE'D"
                                  AND THE LCB CHAIN IS SEARCHED TO
                                  REMOVE THE "CLOSE'D" LCB.  THE
                                  LCB CANNOT BE FOUND ON THE CHAIN
                                  WHICH BEGINS WITH ".MLCB".

                                  VALUE #1= 177777 (END OF CHAIN)
                                  VALUE #2= 177777 OR UDB ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #3= "CLOSE'D" LCB ADDRESS

14031   RLUDB                   A UNIT DEVICE BLOCK (UDB) IS BEING
                                  REMOVED FROM ITS DEVICE CONTROL
                                  TABLE'S (DCT) CHAIN.  IT IS FOUND
                                  TO STILL HAVE A BUFFER ATTACHED
                                  TO IT WHICH IS AN ERROR.

                                  VALUE #1= ADDR OF BH ON UDB
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= TARGET UDB ADDRESS

14032   RLUDB                   SAME PROCEDURE AS "14031" EXCEPT
                                  THAT THE UDB CANNOT BE FOUND ON
                                  THE DCT'S CHAIN.

                                  VALUE #1= 177777
                                  VALUE #2= TARGET UDB
                                  VALUE #3= 177777 (END OF CHAIN)
                                  VALUE #4= ADDR OF LAST UDB IN LIST

14033   NQCCB                   THE SYSTEM IS ATTEMPTING TO CLEAR
                                  AN AREA OF USER CORE FOR A DISK
                                  TRANSFER.  AN ERROR OCCURRED DURING
                                  THE MAPPING PROCESS.

                                  VALUE #1= # WORDS TO CLEAR
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= USER LOGICAL ADDRESS

14034   NQCCB                   SHOULD NEVER OCCUR.  DELETING SPECI-
                                  FIC DATA ELEMENTS IS NOT IMPLEMENTED.

14035   NQCCB                   DURING BUFFER ASSIGNMENT, A BUFFER
                                  THAT HAS BEEN ASSIGNED IS FOUND
                                  TO BE THE SAME AS THE FIRST ALREADY
                                  ON THE FCB.

                                  VALUE #1= BIT MAP REAL FCB ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #2= 1ST FCB BUFFER ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #3= NEWLY ASSIGNED BUFFER

14036   NQCCB                   AOS/VS IS WAITING FOR A BUFFER TO HAVE
                                  ANY I/O IN PROGRESS COMPLETED.
                                  AN I/O ERROR HAS OCCURRED DURING
                                  THE WAIT.

14037   NQCCB                   AOS/VS IS WAITING FOR A FILE TO HAVE
                                  ANY I/O IN PROGRESS COMPLETED.
                                  AN I/O ERROR HAS OCCURRED DURING
                                  THE WAIT.

14040   PPCUS                   AN ERROR OCCURRED WHILE TRYING TO MAP
                                  THE USER TCB INTO THE 64K SLOT.

                                  VALUE #1= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #2= 13 (WORDS IN TCB)
                                  VALUE #3= TCB ADDRESS

14041   NQCCB                   SAME AS "14034".

14042   PPMUS                   SAME AS "14040".

14043   CFAULT                  THE CCBS ARE REQUESTED TO BE LOADED
                                  FROM THE SWAP FILE.  THE CONTENTS
                                  OF THE ADDRESS CONTAINED IN OFFSET
                                  PCBPT OF THE PTABLE EXTENSION IS
                                  NEITHER 0 NOR 177777.  THIS IS AN
                                  ERROR SINCE THE CCBS SHOULD NOT
                                  ALREADY BE IN CORE.

                                  VALUE #1= 4
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= CONTENTS OF CCB POINTER
                                                TABLE ADDRESS
14044   RSMEM                   AOS/VS "GENERAL MEMORY POOL" MEMORY
                                  IS RELEASED AND ACQUIRED IN MULTI-
                                  PLES OF BASE 2 BEGINNING WITH 8
                                  WORDS.  THE LEGITIMATE MULTIPLES
                                  VS "INDEX" ARE:
                                        0 = 8  WORDS
                                        1 = 16   "
                                        2 = 32   "
                                        3 = 64   "
                                        4 = 128  "
                                        5 = 256  "
                                  A CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO RELEASE A
                                  SECTION OF MEMORY WHICH CORRESPONDS
                                  TO AN ILLEGAL INDEX.

                                  VALUE #1=  RESIDUE ABOVE INDEX VALUE
                                  VALUE #2=  ADDR OF SECTION IN AOS/VS
                                  VALUE #3=  ILLEGAL INDEX

14045   GSMEM                   SAME REASONS AS "14044" EXCEPT THAT
                                  ERROR OCCURRED ON ATTEMPTING TO
                                  GET MEMORY.

                                  VALUE #1=  RESIDUE ABOVE INDEX VALUE
                                  VALUE #2=  (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3=  ILLEGAL INDEX

14046   DPFST                   THE ZEBRA (6060/61/67) DISK START-UP
                                  ROUTINE IS ATTEMPTING TO DISPATCH
                                  ON AN ILLEGAL DISK STATE.

                                  VALUE #1= ILLEGAL STATE

14047   BUFIO                   SINCE THERE CAN BE MULTIPLE PHYSICAL
                                  DISKS WITHIN A LOGICAL DISK, EACH
                                  PHYSICAL DISK (UDB) HAS ITS OWN
                                  LOGICAL ADDRESS RANGE.  BUFFER HEADERS
                                  CONTAIN LOGICAL DISK ADDRESSES AND
                                  ARE LINKED ONTO THE PROPER UDB.
                                  THE ADDRESS FOUND IN THE BUF HEADER
                                  IS LARGER THAN ANY UDB ATTACHED TO
                                  THE LD.

                                  VALUE #1= BUFFER LOG DISK ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #2= LAST UNIT # ON LDU(See VALUE 3)
                                  VALUE #3= LAST DEVICE CODE ON LDU

                                  NOTE THAT DISK ADDRESSES ARE DOUBLE
                                  WORD, SO VALUE #1 AND #2 CAN EITHER
                                  BE THE HIGH OR LOW WORD.

14050   NQBHR                   A BUFFER HEADER IS TO BE LINKED ONTO
                                  THE PROPER UDB, BUT IT IS FOUND
                                  THAT ITS "I/O IN PROGRESS" STATUS
                                  BIT IS ALREADY SET.

                                  VALUE #3= BUFFER HEADER MEMORY ADDR

14051   NQBHR                   THE NUMBER OF BLOCKS REQUESTED (BQNBK)
                                  IS FOUND TO BE 0.

14052   IODON                   A REQUEST HAS BEEN MADE TO A LOGICAL
                                  DISK OF MULTIPLE DISK BLOCKS WHOSE
                                  LAST DISK BLOCK IS PAST THE "EOF"
                                  OF THE LD.

14053   DPANQ                   A BUFFER HEADER IS BEING INSERTED INTO
                                  THE BUFFER HEADER CHAIN OFF OF THE
                                  UDB.  IT IS FOUND THAT EITHER THE
                                  PREVIOUS OR NEXT BUFFER HEADER ON
                                  THE CHAIN HAS THE SAME ADDRESS.

                                  VALUE #1= NEXT BUFF HEADER ADDR
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= PREVIOUS BUFF HEADER ADDR

14054   OVCHN                   THE OVERLAY # BEING REQUESTED TO BE
                                  LOADED IS GREATER THAN THE MAXIMUM
                                  OVERLAY # IN THE SYSTEM.

                                  VALUE #1= REQUESTED OVERLAY #
                                  VALUE #2= ENTRY OFFSET INTO OVERLAY
                                  VALUE #3= "OVTAB" ADDRESS

14055   SWIAB                   SAME AS "14002".

14056   FREBF                   SAME AS "14002".

14057   INREL                   A CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO "GMBLK" TO GET
                                  A FREE 1K MEMORY PAGE.   AN ERROR
                                  RETURN WILL BE TAKEN IF THERE ARE
                                  NO FREE MEMORY PAGES ON EITHER THE
                                  "FREE MEMORY CHAIN" OR THE "CANDI-
                                  DATE CHAIN".

14060   INREL                   A CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO "GSMEM" TO GET
                                  AN AREA OF SCRATCH SPACE TO BUILT
                                  EITHER A STACK (400 WDS) OR A CB
                                  (25 WDS).  AN ERROR RETURN WILL BE
                                  TAKEN IF NO MEMORY IS AVAILABLE AND
                                  NO PREEMPTION IS POSSIBLE.

14061   CMINT                   THE CORE REQUEST FLAG WORD IS CHECKED
                                  FOR THE REQUESTED OPERATION VIA "LOB"
                                  AND THEN THAT REQUEST "LDSP" ON.  THE
                                  "LDSP" TABLE OFFSET WAS OUTSIDE THE
                                  TABLE LIMITS.

                                  VALUE #1= TABLE OFFSET

14062   CMINT                   WHEN THE NUMBER OF ENTRIES ON THE
                                  "SHARED PAGE CHAIN" INCREASES BE-
                                  YOND A SPECIFIC VALUE,  ENTRIES
                                  ON THE CHAIN ARE RELEASED.  A COUNTER
                                  INDICATES PAGES ON THE CHAIN BUT
                                  THE POINTER IN THE HEAD OF THE
                                  CHAIN INDICATES NO ENTRIES. 

                                  VALUE #1=  CURRENT # ENTRIES COUNTER
                                  VALUE #2=  MAX ENTRIES ALLOWED
                                  VALUE #3=  "SMFLG" ADDRESS

14063   CMENQ                   A PROCESS IS BEING ENQUEUED TO THE
                                  CORE MANAGER'S QUEUE FOR A SWAP
                                  OUT.  IT IS FOUND THAT THE PROCESS
                                  IS NOT ONLY BOUND TO A VIRTUAL
                                  PROCESSOR BUT MUST REMAIN BOUND TO
                                  A VIRTUAL PROCESSOR.  THIS SHOULD
                                  HAVE BEEN CAUGHT PRIOR TO THIS POINT
                                  IN THE "PRPR" ROUTINE.

                                  VALUE #2= VIRTUAL PTABLE ADDRESS

14064   SINIT                   VSGEN HAS DEFINED A DEVICE WHICH COULD
                                  BE ON THE "HIGH SPEED CHANNEL"(HSC)
                                  BUT AOS/VS DOESN'T KNOW ABOUT IT BECAUSE
                                  OF THE DEFINED DEVICE TYPE (DCTYP).

14065   RELD                    AN AOS/VS INTERNAL CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO
                                  RELEASE A BUFFER AND TO DESTROY ITS
                                  ID.   IT IS FOUND THAT THE BUFFER
                                  HAS A "USE COUNT">1 WHICH IS AN
                                  ERROR.

                                  VALUE #3= BUFFER HEADER ADDRESS

14066   BLKIN                   (REPLACED BY CODE 006345)
                                A CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO "BLKIN" WHICH
                                  IS USED TO READ ONE BLOCK OF A DISK
                                  FILE.  IT IS FOUND THAT THE ID OF
                                  THE CCB AND THE ID OF THE FCB DO NOT
                                  MATCH.

                                  VALUE #1= FCB ID
                                  VALUE #2= CCB ID
                                  VALUE #3= FCB ADDRESS

14067   CULCK                   A CALL HAS BEEN MADE TO UNLOCK A "LOCKED"
                                  CCB.   IT IS FOUND THAT THE "LOCKED"
                                  CCB IS ALREADY UNLOCKED.

                                  VALUE #3= CCB ADDRESS

14070   CMCBV                   THIS ROUTINE HAS BEEN CALLED AND PASSED
                                  THE ADDRESS OF A MAPPED CCB.  IT IS
                                  FOUND THAT THIS ADDRESS IS INVALID.


14071   WRB2                    THESE ROUTINES ARE EXTENSIONS TO THE
                                  WRB/RDB SYSTEM CALLS.  THE CALL HAS
                                  BEEN RESTARTED AND IT IS FOUND THAT
                                  THE HOST ID IS "0".

                                  VALUE #1=  0
                                  VALUE #2=  (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3=  TCB ADDRESS + 76000 THAT
                                                MADE SYSTEM CALL

                                  THE "HOST ID" IS CONTAINED IN BITS
                                  1-7 OF ?TAC1 WHICH CONTAINS THE
                                  USER CHANNEL #.  THE OVERLAY "IOOV"
                                  SHOULD HAVE PREVIOUSLY CHECKED THE
                                  HOST ID FOR VALIDITY.


14072           CWAKE           THIS ROUTINE HAS BEEN CALLED AND PASSED
                                  A BIT NUMBER (TO BE SET IN SMFLG).
                                  IT HAS BEEN FOUND THAT THE BIT IS 
                                  INVALID.

14073           ROVCL           ROVCL HAS BEEN CALLED TO TRANSFER CONTROL
                                  TO A RESIDENT OVERLAY WHICH WAS NOT
                                  LOADED AT SINIT TIME.

                                  VALUE #1=  ZERO RELATIVE RESIDENT
                                                OVERLAY NUMBER
                                  VALUE #2=  CRSEG VALUE
                                  VALUE #3=  RDHDR+CMOV1 VALUE
                                  VALUE #4=  RETURN ADDRESS OF ROVCL

                                THESE VALUES CAN BE USED TO PATCH THE
                                  SYSTEM TO PREVENT THIS FROM HAPPENING.
                                  ROVTB+(VALUE #1) SHOULD BE SET TO 1.
                                  THE OTHER VALUES ARE USEFUL IN DETERMINING
                                  FROM WHERE THE BOGUS CALL CAME.

14074           RPMUS           AN ERROR OCCURED WHILE TRYING TO MAP
                                  A USER'S AC2.

                                  VALUE #1=  PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #2=  1
                                  VALUE #3=  ADDRESS OF AC2 IN TCB

14075           RPMUS           AN ERROR OCCURED WHILE TRYING TO MAP
                                  A USER'S PACKET.

                                  VALUE #1=  PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS
                                  VALUE #2=  1
                                  VALUE #3=  ADDRESS OF PACKET+?PRNH

14076           RELD            AN AOS/VS INTERNAL CALL HAS BEEN
                                  MADE TO RELEASE A BUFFER AND
                                  DESTROY ITS ID.  IT IS FOUND
                                  THAT THE MODIFIED BIT IS ON,
                                  MEANING THAT SOME OTHER CODE
                                  PATH HAS ALREADY RELEASED THE
                                  BUFFER TO BE FLUSHED TO DISK.
                                  THIS IS AN ERROR BECAUSE THE
                                  ID CANNOT BE DESTROYED BEFORE
                                  THE BUFFER HAS BEEN FLUSHED
                                  TO THE DISK.

                                  VALUE #3= BUFFER HEADER ADDRESS
14077           MAPVP           A CALL TO MAPVP TO MAP IN A VIRTUAL
                                  CHUNK OF SYSTEM MEMORY HAS BEEN
                                  MADE. THE VIRTUAL ADDRESS PASSED
                                  IN IS NOT WITHIN THE LEGAL LIMITS
                                  FOR THE CURRENTLY RUNNING SYSTEM.


                                  VALUE #1= PAGE REQUESTED
                                  VALUE #2= HIGHEST LEGAL PAGE
                                  VALUE #3= LOWEST LEGAL PAGE

14100           WDCBK           AN ATTEMPT TO TURN ON SOME BITS IN
                                  THE BITMAP HAS BEEN MADE, BUT SOME
                                  OF THE BITS ARE ALREADY ON.

                                  VALUE #1= PREVIOUS CONTENTS OF WORD
                                  VALUE #2= CONTENTS TO BE IOR'ED IN
                                  VALUE #3= MEMORY ADDRESS OF WORD

14101           WDCBK           SAME AS PANIC  14100

14102           WDCBK           SAME AS PANIC  14100

14103           SCHED           ON INCREMENTING THE ACTIVE CALL COUNT
                                FOR A PROCESS THE CURRENT CALL COUNT
                                (PSQCT) IS FOUND TO BE NEGATIVE

                                VALUE #1= 'DONT MAKE VIRTUAL' BIT PTR
                                VALUE #2= POINTER FOR LMP
                                VALUE #3= PROCESS TABLE ADDRESS  OF
                                         PROCESS WHOSE COUNT IS ISZ'D

14104           ECC             WHEN TRYING TO CORRECT AN ECC ERROR,
                                THE VALUE WE GOT OUT OF A BUFFER HEADER
