PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -----------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 15 ******

15001     PFL                   THIS PANIC WILL OCCUR AFTER A POWER
                                  FAILURE ON "POWER UP" AND WILL ONLY
                                  BE SEEN ON A CPU THAT WAS IN "LOCK"
                                  WHICH HAD CORE MEMORY OR MOS MEMORY
                                  WITH BATTERY BACKUP ( AND THE BATT-
                                  ERIES HAD NOT RUN DOWN ).


PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 17 ******

17001   IOPDR                   THE PMGR IN THE IOP WILL INTERRUPT
                                  THE HOST WHEN IT NEEDS THE HOST TO
                                  DO WORK FOR IT.  IT WILL PASS A
                                  "FUNCTION CODE" TO THE HOST WHICH
                                  SPECIFIES THE NEEDED JOB.  THE LEGAL
                                  FUNCTION CODES ARE:
                                        1 = HANDLE INTERRUPT SEQUENCE
                                        2 = HANDLE MODEM DISCONNECT
                                        3 = CON0 INPUT START
                                        4 = CON0 OUTPUT START
                                  THIS PANIC INDICATES THAT AN ILLEGAL
                                  FUNCTION CODE HAS BEEN PASSED FROM
                                  THE IOPMGR.

                                  VALUE #1=  ILLEGAL FUNCTION CODE

17002   IOPDR/IACDR             THE PMGR IN THE IOP/IAC WILL PASS A
                                PANIC CODE TO THE HOST AND "HALT"
                                WHEN IT FINDS A CONDITION THAT IT
                                CANNOT RESOLVE.

                                  VALUE #1 = IOP/IAC  ERROR CODE
                                  VALUE #2 = IAC DEVICE CODE (0 - 177)
                                  VALUE #3 = IOPMGR PC @ PANIC

                                  THE DEFINITIONS FOR THE "IOPMGR ERROR
                                  CODE" CAN BE FOUND IN THIS DOCUMENT
                                  IN A TABLE AT THE END OF THE PANIC
                                  12 SECTION.  THESE CODES PERTAIN TO
                                  BOTH PANIC 12'S AND PANIC 17'S.

17003   TTISR                   THE IOP HAS TIMED OUT WHILE THE HOST
                                  IS WAITING FOR THE CON0 CHARACTER
                                  ACKNOWLEDGEMENT

AOS/VS SPECIFIC CODES

17300   IOPDR                   THE IOP/IAC HAS PASSED AN INVALID
                                  COMPLETION WORD TO THE HOST.
17301   PERDR                   THE IOP/IAC HAS BEEN TIMED FOR ROUGHLY
                                  5 SECONDS WITHOUT UNLOCKING ITS
                                  WORD OF THE HOST/IOP LOCK.  THIS
                                  WOULD NORMALLY INDICATE THAT THE
                                  IOP/IAC HAS STOPPED OR IS LOOPING.
PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -------------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 20 ******

20001   IOPDR                   THE IOP HAS CAUSED AN UNSCHEDULED
                                  (NOT PROGRAMMED) INTERRUPT.  THIS
                                  MUST BE CAUSED BY AN IOP MEMORY
                                  PARITY ERROR.

                                  VALUE #1= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #2= (NOT RELEVANT)
                                  VALUE #3= PC OF IOPMGR AT THE TIME
                                                OF PARITY ERROR

                                  THE ADDRESS OF THE LOCATION THAT
                                  CAUSED THE PARITY ERROR IS NOT
                                  AVAILABLE FROM THE HARDWARE.

PANIC   ROUTINE         PANIC DESCRIPTION
-----   -------         -----------------------------------

;****** PANIC CODE 22 ******

        22000 PANICS ARE CPU FATAL ERROR CONDITIONS REPORTED
                OVER DC 45 INTERFACE ON MV SERIES CPUS


22300           SCPIS           IOC PARITY ERROR REPORTED

22301           SCPIS           OVER TEMPERATURE ALARM REPORTED

22302           SCPIS           SCP-OS NOTIFIED AOS/VS OF A MULTI-BIT
                                ERCC (HARD) ERROR AND AOS/VS COULD NOT
                                RECOVER FROM THE CONDITION.
                                VALUE #1 = CAUSE (1= SNIFF, 2=UNCERTAIN,
                                        4=I/O, OR 10=CPU ACCESS)
                                VALUE #2 = SCP EVENT CODE (54 OR 55)

                                VALUE #5 = ACCESS CODE (SAME AS #1)
                                VALUE #6 = PHYSICAL PAGE # OF ERCC HIT
                                VALUE #7 = DOUBLE WORD ON MODULE
                                VALUE #8 = SYNDROME BITS

22303           SCPIS           SCP-OS NOTIFIED AOS/VS OF A PARITY ERROR
                                IN MEMORY (FOR PARITY MEMORY MACHINES
                                ONLY, I.E. MV/2000)

                                VALUE #5 = SCP EVENT CODE (210 OCTAL)
                                VALUE #6 = PHYSICAL PAGE #
                                VALUE #7 = NOT USED
                                VALUE #8 = NOT USED

