;*****  PANIC CODE 27 *****

;Ring 0 TSWVTA library



;*****  PANIC CODE 30 *****

;Ring 0 TSH(RING 0 PMGR) library

;****************************************************************************
;
;    The following panic's were generated by a call to tsh_panic which pushes 
; various arguments onto the stack and then calls k$_panic. The values 
; displayed correspond to the following index unless noted otherwise.
;       
;               value 1 = panic code
;               value 2 = frame pointer
;               value 3 = stack pointer
;               value 4 = stack base
;               value 5 = stack limit
;               value 6 = AC3 = PC
;               value 7 = AC2
;               value 8 = AC1
;               value 9 = AC0
;
;****************************************************************************

30001                                   A failure has occured at either
                                        tshX_init in TSH_INIT.SR or tsh_bldhpb
                                        in tsh_init_utils.c If the error has
                                        occured at tsh_bldhpb the panic code
                                        and value 1 will be 30001. A call 
                                        to k$_pool_create failed. No memory was
                                        available for the PIB.
                                        If the error occured at tshX_init then
                                        an attempt to create memory pools for
                                        a PIB, SSA, or SOA has failed. A call
                                        from TSH_INIT.SR to tsh_create_pool 
                                        and subsequent call to k$_pool_create
                                        was unsuccessfull.

                                        value 1: error code from k$_pool_create
                                   
30002                                   tshX_init has failed in TSH_INIT.SR.
                                        An attempt to create a lock has failed.
                                        A call to tsh_create_lock and it's sub-
                                        -sequent call to tsh_gmem was not
                                        successfull. 

                                        value 1: error code from 
                                                 k$_block_allocate

30003                                   tsh_build_per_entry has failed in
                                        tsh_init_utils.c. Value 2 indicates the
                                        cause of the failure.

                                        value 1 = 1: tsh_current_ctlr_table_ptr
                                                ->per_file_type = 0. The file 
                                                type for the :PER entry is not
                                                defined.

                                        value 1 = 2: A call to kfs$_file_create
                                                to create the :PER entry has
                                                failed. 

                                        value 1 = 3: A call to kfs$_file_create
                                                to create a link to CON0 has
                                                failed.

30004                                   Bad port on INIT PIB's

30005                                   tshX_init has failed in TSH_INIT.SR.
                                        The device initialization has failed.
                                        Either there is no initialization
                                        address ( = 0 ) or the device type
                                        is not within limits.

30006                                   Error on LPHY

30007                                   A KVS or MKP call has failed.
                                        An error has occured in either
                                        TSH_MKPUTIL.SR, TSH_CLOSE.SR or
                                        tsh_process_opcon_msg().
                                        If the error is in TSH_MKPUTIL.SR
                                        a k$_ or kvs$_ call has failed.
                                        If the error is in TSH_CLOSE.SR
                                        a tsh routine in that module has
                                        taken an error. The failing routine
                                        may or may not have a subsequent
                                        call to k$_ or kvs$_. If the error
                                        is in tsh_process_opcon_msg a call
                                        to k$_send_ipc() has failed and the 
                                        following values apply:
                                        
                                            value 1 = error code from call
                                            value 2 = routine that failed
                                                (k$_send_ipc())
                                            value 3 = routine issuing call
                                                (tsh_process_opcon_msg())
                                            value 4 = ARG. 1 of k$_send_ipc
                                                (senders pid = 0)
                                            value 5 = ARG. 2 of k$_send_ipc
                                                (senders ring = 0)
                                            value 6 = ARG. 3 of k$_send_ipc
                                                (address of send header)
                                            value 7 = status returned from
                                                k$_send_ipc() call.

30010                                   Fatal Validity Trap

30011                                   An illegal memory request has occured.
                                        Either TSH_INIT.SR or TSH_MKPUTIL.SR
                                        has failed.
                                        In TSH_INIT.SR tshX_init has failed.
                                        The size of a TEMP buffer allocated on
